---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { FileText, ArrowLeft, Mail, Globe } from 'lucide-astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Terms of Service — DevStackHub" 
  description="Terms of Service, intellectual property rights, and operational disclosures for DevStackHub."
>
  <Header />

  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-32 pb-24">
    <div class="mb-8">
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 hover:underline">
        <ArrowLeft class="w-3.5 h-3.5" /> Return to Home
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-mono font-semibold bg-emerald-500/10 text-emerald-400 border border-emerald-500/20 mb-4">
      <FileText class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-emerald-400" />
      <span>OPERATIONAL POLICY</span>
    </div>

    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
      Terms of Service
    </h1>
    <p class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-500 mt-2">Last Updated: August 2026</p>

    <div class="prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert prose-emerald max-w-none mt-10 space-y-6 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Welcome to <strong>DevStackHub</strong> (<a href="https://devstackhub.tech" class="text-emerald-400 hover:underline">devstackhub.tech</a>). By accessing or using our website, tutorials, technical guides, code snippets, and newsletter, you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree with any part of these terms, please discontinue use of the site.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mt-8 border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">1. Intellectual Property & Permitted Use</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
        <li><strong>Original Content:</strong> All articles, guides, custom architectural diagrams, branding, and written materials published on DevStackHub are the intellectual property of DevStackHub unless otherwise stated.</li>
        <li><strong>Code Snippets & Configurations:</strong> Configuration files, scripts (e.g., YAML, Dockerfiles, Terraform scripts, Bash commands), and technical code snippets provided in our tutorials are free to use, modify, and integrate into your personal or commercial software projects.</li>
        <li><strong>Reproduction Restrictions:</strong> You may not scrape, republish, or redistribute entire articles or extensive portions of our written editorial content on other websites or platforms without explicit written consent.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mt-8 border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">2. Technical Disclaimers & "As-Is" Provision</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
        <li><strong>Educational Purpose:</strong> The content, deployment playbooks, and architectural guides on DevStackHub are provided strictly for educational and informational purposes.</li>
        <li><strong>No Warranty:</strong> While we strive to publish accurate, production-tested configurations, all software, tools, and code examples are provided on an <strong>"as-is"</strong> and <strong>"as-available"</strong> basis without warranties of any kind, express or implied.</li>
        <li><strong>Infrastructure Liability:</strong> You are solely responsible for verifying, testing, and securing any code or cloud configurations in isolated staging environments before deploying them to live production systems. DevStackHub shall not be held liable for any data loss, service downtime, cloud billing overages, or security vulnerabilities resulting from the use of our guides.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mt-8 border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">3. External Links & Third-Party Services</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
        <li>Our tutorials frequently link to third-party tools, official documentation (such as GitHub, Docker, and Microsoft Azure), and cloud service providers.</li>
        <li>DevStackHub has no control over the content, uptime, privacy policies, or practices of third-party websites and assumes no responsibility for them.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mt-8 border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">4. Affiliate & Advertising Disclosure</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
        <li>DevStackHub may participate in technical affiliate marketing programs and display contextual advertising networks. Some outbound links to developer tools, cloud hosting platforms, or SaaS services may be affiliate links.</li>
        <li>If you click an affiliate link and make a purchase or create a paid account, DevStackHub may earn a commission at no additional cost to you. We only recommend platforms and tools that align with our engineering standards.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mt-8 border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">5. User Conduct</h2>
      <p>When interacting with the website, you agree not to:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
        <li>Attempt to disrupt, overload, or compromise the security and performance of our web servers.</li>
        <li>Transmit any malicious code, automated spam, or unauthorized promotional material.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mt-8 border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">6. Modifications to Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We reserve the right to revise and update these Terms of Service at any time. Any changes will be posted directly to this page with an updated revision date. Your continued use of the website following any modifications signifies your acceptance of the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mt-8 border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">7. Contact Information</h2>
      <p>If you have any questions or legal inquiries regarding these Terms of Service, please contact us:</p>
      <ul class="list-none pl-0 space-y-2 font-mono text-xs">
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <Globe class="w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400" />
          <span>Website: <a href="https://devstackhub.tech/contact/" class="text-emerald-400 hover:underline">https://devstackhub.tech/contact/</a></span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <Mail class="w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400" />
          <span>Email: <a href="mailto:contact@devstackhub.tech" class="text-emerald-400 hover:underline">contact@devstackhub.tech</a></span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>